# 9. OUTSIDER ELIGIBILITY SYSTEM

Every event must explicitly specify who can participate.

Support these eligibility types:
- Society Members Only.
- Organising College Students Only.
- Selected Colleges Only.
- All IPU College Students.
- All College Students.
- Open to Outsiders.
- Public Event.
- Custom Eligibility.

Allow organisers to add a short eligibility explanation.

Examples:
- "Open to students from all colleges."
- "Only registered society members can participate."
- "Open to non-members; external college students may register."
- "Open to the public. Valid registration required."

IMPORTANT:
- Do not infer outsider eligibility using AI alone.
- The event organiser must select and confirm the eligibility.
- If eligibility is missing, show "Eligibility not confirmed."
- If the event is restricted, display the restriction clearly before the registration button.
- Do not imply that a successful online registration guarantees entry to the venue.
- Where college ID or other verification is required, show the requirement before submission.

